            <ArticleTitle>Isolated Proximal Tibiofibular Dislocation during Soccer.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>657581</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1155/2015/657581</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Proximal tibiofibular dislocations are rarely encountered in the Emergency Department (ED). We present a case involving a man presenting to the ED with left knee pain after making a sharp left turn on the soccer field. His physical exam was only remarkable for tenderness over the lateral fibular head. His X-rays showed subtle abnormalities of the tibiofibular joint. The dislocation was reduced and the patient was discharged from the ED with orthopedic follow-up.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
